00:35:17,747 --> 00:35:19,777
I personally love shepherd's purse.

787
00:35:20,317 --> 00:35:23,287
Shepherd's purse hides here and there.

788
00:35:23,447 --> 00:35:25,656
When I dig up shepherd's purse...

789
00:35:25,657 --> 00:35:27,516
I don't know if I feel that way since it's my own work,

790
00:35:27,517 --> 00:35:29,427
but it tastes much more tender.

791
00:35:30,287 --> 00:35:33,197
So I dug up shepherd's purse diligently...

792
00:35:33,697 --> 00:35:36,497
in order to make doenjang jjigae.

793
00:35:39,097 --> 00:35:41,666
You can find an entire group when there's one.

794
00:35:41,667 --> 00:35:43,837
(You can find an entire group when there's one.)

795
00:35:44,907 --> 00:35:47,636
(He collects shepherd's purse amidst similar-looking grass.)

796
00:35:47,637 --> 00:35:48,707
How fascinating.

797
00:35:51,677 --> 00:35:53,117
Gosh, the root got cut off.

798
00:35:54,947 --> 00:35:57,387
- The root has all the nutrients. - It looks like moss.

799
00:35:57,787 --> 00:35:59,687
You wouldn't recognize it if you hadn't dug it up before.

800
00:35:59,957 --> 00:36:01,956
- You've done it since childhood. - That's right.

801
00:36:01,957 --> 00:36:03,386
- Yes. - That's why you can spot it.

802
00:36:03,387 --> 00:36:05,797
- I see. - My grandma raised me.

803
00:36:06,957 --> 00:36:09,627
So I naturally had such experiences.

804
00:36:10,697 --> 00:36:13,467
(He goes in search of the next shepherd's purse.)

805
00:36:14,397 --> 00:36:16,737
The first characteristic is...

806
00:36:17,467 --> 00:36:19,037
that it's really close to the ground.

807
00:36:19,237 --> 00:36:22,047
The leaves stick to the ground.

808
00:36:22,207 --> 00:36:23,777
That's one characteristic.

809
00:36:23,907 --> 00:36:26,716
The most confusing thing is that there's one similar-looking weed.

810
00:36:26,717 --> 00:36:28,186
I don't know what that weed is.

811
00:36:28,187 --> 00:36:31,387
But the back side of that weed is white.

812
00:36:31,687 --> 00:36:33,357
If the back side is white, it isn't shepherd's purse.

813
00:36:34,287 --> 00:36:35,686
That's the difference.

814
00:36:35,687 --> 00:36:37,556
You're right. I see what you mean.

815
00:36:37,557 --> 00:36:39,896
That weed doesn't stick to the ground.

816
00:36:39,897 --> 00:36:41,666
The leaves point upward.

817
00:36:41,667 --> 00:36:42,926
(Unlike shepherd's purse, its leaves point upward.)

818
00:36:42,927 --> 00:36:46,266
Lastly, shepherd's purse is never alone.

819
00:36:46,267 --> 00:36:47,367
Is it with someone?

820
00:36:47,537 --> 00:36:49,667
When you find one shepherd's purse,

821
00:36:49,837 --> 00:36:53,037
you'll find its friends nearby.

822
00:36:53,207 --> 00:36:54,437
- They live as a group. - Yes.

823
00:36:55,347 --> 00:36:57,677
Shepherd's purse has such characteristics.

824
00:36:59,047 --> 00:37:00,477
There are so many.

825
00:37:01,747 --> 00:37:03,187
He's like Little Tiger.

826
00:37:03,647 --> 00:37:05,186
- You're right. - He has that side.

827
00:37:05,187 --> 00:37:06,457
- He's the male version. - What is it?

828
00:37:09,287 --> 00:37:10,627
It looks fun.

829
00:37:10,857 --> 00:37:11,927
It's therapeutic.

830
00:37:12,027 --> 00:37:13,697
- I bet. It's therapeutic to watch. - It's so big.

831
00:37:14,727 --> 00:37:17,326
(Digging up shepherd's purse gives him a therapeutic moment.)

832
00:37:17,327 --> 00:37:19,367
His snot looks like dew.

833
00:37:19,397 --> 00:37:20,397
(Dangling)

834
00:37:20,398 --> 00:37:21,466
I can't believe you spotted it.

835
00:37:21,467 --> 00:37:23,466
- It looks fine since it's clear. - It's very clear.

836
00:37:23,467 --> 00:37:26,107
- Thank goodness. - Usually, it's sticky.

837
00:37:27,037 --> 00:37:28,646
I've never seen a man with such clear snot.

838
00:37:28,647 --> 00:37:30,046
- That's right. - It doesn't look very dirty.

839
00:37:30,047 --> 00:37:31,616
- I'm glad. - It doesn't look very dirty.

840
00:37:31,617 --> 00:37:33,616
- It's like dew. - It almost looks like sweat.

841
00:37:33,617 --> 00:37:35,047
(In Hyuk's snot can't be clearer.)

842
00:37:35,387 --> 00:37:37,517
Let's go.

843
00:37:38,617 --> 00:37:40,457
(Groaning)

844
00:37:40,757 --> 00:37:43,356
(Aching)

845
00:37:43,357 --> 00:37:45,256
You look a bit tired.

846
00:37:45,257 --> 00:37:46,557
It was exhausting indeed.

847
00:37:47,157 --> 00:37:48,866
I put too much effort into the concert.

848
00:37:48,867 --> 00:37:52,696
Fate in time

849
00:37:52,697 --> 00:37:54,336
It's natural to be exhausted after the concert.

850
00:37:54,337 --> 00:37:55,767
That's right. It was after the concert.

851
00:37:57,667 --> 00:38:00,037
- It's still therapeutic, right? - It's very therapeutic.

852
00:38:00,737 --> 00:38:02,547
(Sniffling)

853
00:38:04,407 --> 00:38:05,577
It's enough.

854
00:38:06,177 --> 00:38:07,277
He dug up a lot.

855
00:38:07,717 --> 00:38:10,287
You can season it or add it to doenjang jjigae.

856
00:38:10,947 --> 00:38:12,016
(Upon return, he enters the garden inside the yard.)

857
00:38:12,017 --> 00:38:14,286
There's so much to work on.

858
00:38:14,287 --> 00:38:15,287
(Upon return, he enters the garden inside the yard.)

859
00:38:15,627 --> 00:38:19,027
(Looking around)

860
00:38:21,627 --> 00:38:23,297
This is goldmoss stonecrop.

861
00:38:23,767 --> 00:38:24,866
What was that?

862
00:38:24,867 --> 00:38:26,836
- Does it grow on stone? - It's my first time seeing that.

863
00:38:26,837 --> 00:38:29,306
Goldmoss stonecrop has different names...

864
00:38:29,307 --> 00:38:30,836
