926
00:40:59,261 --> 00:41:00,860
The bellflower roots?

927
00:41:00,861 --> 00:41:02,030
(Enough is taken out for their meal.)

928
00:41:02,031 --> 00:41:04,360
They're all setting everything up naturally.

929
00:41:04,361 --> 00:41:07,031
We all eat together often at my family's house.

930
00:41:07,331 --> 00:41:08,631
The meat must be of good quality.

931
00:41:09,401 --> 00:41:10,831
Friends are the best.

932
00:41:12,001 --> 00:41:14,200
Won't it take long to make the jjigae?

933
00:41:14,201 --> 00:41:15,411
The jjigae won't take long.

934
00:41:15,941 --> 00:41:17,981
(Meanwhile,)

935
00:41:18,511 --> 00:41:21,611
(In Hyuk is washing the shepherd's purse he collected.)

936
00:41:24,581 --> 00:41:26,180
Gosh, there's so much dirt.

937
00:41:26,181 --> 00:41:28,520
There's a lot of dirt on the ends.

938
00:41:28,521 --> 00:41:30,050
- Right. - They have to be washed thoroughly.

939
00:41:30,051 --> 00:41:31,660
- They have to be washed a lot. - They have to be washed a lot.

940
00:41:31,661 --> 00:41:32,860
- Right. - You might feel the dust.

941
00:41:32,861 --> 00:41:34,260
(Washing over and over)

942
00:41:34,261 --> 00:41:35,560
He's diligent.

943
00:41:35,561 --> 00:41:36,631
(Washing over and over)

944
00:41:37,061 --> 00:41:40,101
(The dirt is removed after repeating it many times.)

945
00:41:40,461 --> 00:41:42,071
There we go. This should be clean enough.

946
00:41:42,531 --> 00:41:45,241
This much dirt is fine. We all grew up eating dirt.

947
00:41:45,401 --> 00:41:46,601
That will bust up your appendix.

948
00:41:47,711 --> 00:41:49,611
It feels like your cooking will be really good.

949
00:41:49,771 --> 00:41:51,181
I cook fairly often.

950
00:41:51,911 --> 00:41:53,511
The shepherd's purse doenjang jjigae is really easy.

951
00:41:54,751 --> 00:41:56,181
The shepherd's purse is put into the pot.

952
00:41:56,451 --> 00:42:00,021
A big spoonful and a half or two big spoonfuls are put in.

953
00:42:00,651 --> 00:42:02,090
(And frying powder?)

954
00:42:02,091 --> 00:42:03,620
Frying powder is added in.

955
00:42:03,621 --> 00:42:05,461
What? In there?

956
00:42:06,061 --> 00:42:08,160
Originally, when shepherd's purse doenjang jjigae is made,

957
00:42:08,161 --> 00:42:12,661
I heard that rice water should be used to make it light and thick.

958
00:42:13,331 --> 00:42:16,001
But adding in frying powder or flour...

959
00:42:16,631 --> 00:42:18,770
makes it really light...

960
00:42:18,771 --> 00:42:20,700
and it makes the texture feel thick.

961
00:42:20,701 --> 00:42:22,540
That is why I use them.

962
00:42:22,541 --> 00:42:23,671
I see.

963
00:42:24,541 --> 00:42:27,751
Minced garlic brings up its flavor a lot more.

964
00:42:28,651 --> 00:42:30,411
These are really spicy peppers.

965
00:42:30,511 --> 00:42:32,350
I add the pepper and green onion...

966
00:42:32,351 --> 00:42:34,421
to make the soup have a refreshing taste.

967
00:42:35,121 --> 00:42:38,060
It's done once the tofu is added.

968
00:42:38,061 --> 00:42:39,221
It's really easy, isn't it?

969
00:42:39,591 --> 00:42:41,390
Gosh, shepherd's purse. It looks really good.

970
00:42:41,391 --> 00:42:42,391
(The natural shepherd's purse doenjang jjigae is ready.)

971
00:42:42,591 --> 00:42:45,560
As I have lived alone for a while, I got sick of food delivery.

972
00:42:45,561 --> 00:42:46,630
(The cooking skills of the one who has lived alone for 13 years)

973
00:42:46,631 --> 00:42:47,970
I make my own meals quite often.

974
00:42:47,971 --> 00:42:49,301
- You're a great cook. - It looks delicious.

975
00:42:50,531 --> 00:42:52,900
He throws everything in as he cooks.

976
00:42:52,901 --> 00:42:53,901
- I can tell he's a great cook. - Can you tell?

977
00:42:53,902 --> 00:42:54,941
Of course.

978
00:42:57,271 --> 00:42:59,711
The second dish is the goldmoss stonecrop salad.

979
00:42:59,941 --> 00:43:02,550
It can be made easily with some chojang...

980
00:43:02,551 --> 00:43:04,051
