981
00:43:04,181 --> 00:43:05,420
He's a great cook.

982
00:43:05,421 --> 00:43:07,321
(Meanwhile, his friends are almost done with grilling the meat.)

983
00:43:07,481 --> 00:43:09,390
- Gosh, it smells great. - The kimchi looks insane.

984
00:43:09,391 --> 00:43:10,751
Gosh, that looks good!

985
00:43:11,421 --> 00:43:12,490
Shepherd's purse doenjang jjigae.

986
00:43:12,491 --> 00:43:13,520
(In Hyuk's vegetable dishes are served as well.)

987
00:43:13,521 --> 00:43:15,691
(I'm hungry.)

988
00:43:16,231 --> 00:43:17,331
You went through so much, In Hyuk.

989
00:43:20,661 --> 00:43:21,730
(He takes a bite...)

990
00:43:21,731 --> 00:43:22,801
(of the shepherd's purse doenjang jjigae first.)

991
00:43:23,471 --> 00:43:24,971
(Satisfied)

992
00:43:27,941 --> 00:43:28,941
(Groaning)

993
00:43:32,541 --> 00:43:33,941
It's good, isn't it?

994
00:43:35,981 --> 00:43:38,621
(He takes a bite and nods without saying anything.)

995
00:43:40,581 --> 00:43:42,251
They really must be close friends.

996
00:43:43,491 --> 00:43:45,120
- They won't talk. - They won't talk.

997
00:43:45,121 --> 00:43:46,160
They won't even catch up with each other.

998
00:43:46,161 --> 00:43:47,221
Close friends don't do that.

999
00:43:47,491 --> 00:43:49,230
It won't be weird if they leave after finishing their meal.

1000
00:43:49,231 --> 00:43:50,430
- That can happen. - Without saying a word.

1001
00:43:50,431 --> 00:43:52,401
- They won't even say bye. - Right.

1002
00:43:53,561 --> 00:43:55,071
- One is missing after the meal. - Right.

1003
00:43:58,071 --> 00:44:01,270
The shepherd's purse tastes refreshing.

1004
00:44:01,271 --> 00:44:02,811
- Isn't it really soft? - Yes.

1005
00:44:04,011 --> 00:44:07,981
Our Jeonju friends came over to my place in Seoul.

1006
00:44:09,011 --> 00:44:10,781
Was the braised chicken better or is this better?

1007
00:44:10,911 --> 00:44:11,951
This.

1008
00:44:12,781 --> 00:44:14,181
This is way better. I'm serious.

1009
00:44:15,091 --> 00:44:17,591
Tofu and kimchi, potato jeon, and braised chicken.

1010
00:44:17,961 --> 00:44:19,221
We had many different things.

1011
00:44:19,321 --> 00:44:20,520
But this is the best for me.

1012
00:44:20,521 --> 00:44:21,961
- Right. - It's really good.

1013
00:44:22,291 --> 00:44:23,491
It's nice and refreshing.

1014
00:44:26,001 --> 00:44:29,301
I felt really proud as they really enjoyed it.

1015
00:44:30,231 --> 00:44:31,640
- Try some of this as well. - What is that?

1016
00:44:31,641 --> 00:44:32,901
- Did you make it a salad? - Yes.

1017
00:44:34,201 --> 00:44:36,241
(He picks up some of the goldmoss stonecrop salad.)

1018
00:44:36,741 --> 00:44:38,011
You've seen this in restaurants, right?

1019
00:44:38,141 --> 00:44:39,741
