1584
01:05:55,351 --> 01:05:57,090
It's so pretty. How cute.

1585
01:05:57,091 --> 01:06:00,060
(It's been long since he's forgotten Hue-terior.)

1586
01:06:00,061 --> 01:06:01,191
This is cute.

1587
01:06:01,391 --> 01:06:03,291
This is so pretty. It's driving me crazy.

1588
01:06:04,161 --> 01:06:05,631
It's so pretty.

1589
01:06:07,501 --> 01:06:09,101
(The final sweep)

1590
01:06:10,701 --> 01:06:11,771
Let's get going.

1591
01:06:20,081 --> 01:06:21,581
This is how it's done, right?

1592
01:06:32,991 --> 01:06:34,121
It's scary.

1593
01:06:34,721 --> 01:06:36,190
- How bizarre. - How come he's so greedy...

1594
01:06:36,191 --> 01:06:37,661
about everything?

1595
01:06:39,861 --> 01:06:41,101
This is how it's done, right?

1596
01:06:43,471 --> 01:06:45,070
I don't see anyone purchasing items like me.

1597
01:06:45,071 --> 01:06:46,470
- It's hilarious. - I kept turning...

1598
01:06:46,471 --> 01:06:47,471
because it was too heavy.

1599
01:06:49,811 --> 01:06:51,941
How much will these cost? Darn.

1600
01:06:54,641 --> 01:06:55,680
How do I do it?

1601
01:06:55,681 --> 01:06:57,180
(It's finally time to pay.)

1602
01:06:57,181 --> 01:06:59,451
It'll take you forever to pay for them.

1603
01:07:01,221 --> 01:07:03,521
It's like back when I first opened my studio.

1604
01:07:03,751 --> 01:07:04,950
Right. You buy things like that...

1605
01:07:04,951 --> 01:07:06,361
- when you open a studio. - Right.

1606
01:07:07,661 --> 01:07:11,130
(Scanning barcodes as if he'll open a studio)

1607
01:07:11,131 --> 01:07:12,801
This is mine too? Wait, whose is this?

1608
01:07:13,031 --> 01:07:14,431
Oh, it's not mine. Is it?

1609
01:07:15,801 --> 01:07:16,871
Are all these mine?

1610
01:07:17,401 --> 01:07:20,101
Hue Park has a great influence on me.

1611
01:07:20,371 --> 01:07:21,701
You're suddenly blaming me.

1612
01:07:22,301 --> 01:07:23,441
I got lots of Hue-style items.

1613
01:07:24,671 --> 01:07:27,481
I think it'll be pretty if you place those items in an empty space.

1614
01:07:27,811 --> 01:07:29,410
Kian84, you know a thing or two.

1615
01:07:29,411 --> 01:07:31,451
- Painters get each other. - Of course.

1616
01:07:32,081 --> 01:07:34,181
You should go to Japan to meet Ito Junji soon.

1617
01:07:35,921 --> 01:07:37,321
You're going to steal my idol now?

1618
01:07:37,791 --> 01:07:39,491
- Stealing an idol? - I'll tell him I like him more.

1619
01:07:41,721 --> 01:07:43,061
Gosh, I'm so tired. How much is it?

1620
01:07:44,491 --> 01:07:45,631
What?

1621
01:07:46,061 --> 01:07:47,130
It's 1,400 dollars.

1622
01:07:47,131 --> 01:07:48,231
It's 1,400 dollars?

1623
01:07:50,071 --> 01:07:52,401
- You can rack up points too. - Okay.

1624
01:07:56,341 --> 01:07:57,540
- The receipt is so long. - Gosh.

1625
01:07:57,541 --> 01:07:59,481
(Surprised)

1626
01:07:59,881 --> 01:08:01,640
(A never-ending receipt)

1627
01:08:01,641 --> 01:08:03,550
- I bought this many? - It's not like it's a supermarket.

1628
01:08:03,551 --> 01:08:05,211
(A never-ending receipt)

1629
01:08:06,151 --> 01:08:09,350
(Slow)

1630
01:08:09,351 --> 01:08:10,391
It's "Special Mission Dad's Challenge."

1631
01:08:11,021 --> 01:08:12,420
Will all of them fit in your car?

1632
01:08:12,421 --> 01:08:13,920
- They will. - They will?

1633
01:08:13,921 --> 01:08:14,921
(Managing to move with two carts)

1634
01:08:14,922 --> 01:08:16,060
I won't get to try...

1635
01:08:16,061 --> 01:08:17,791
- the 70-cent ice cream. - That one's good, though.

1636
01:08:17,991 --> 01:08:19,800
- I know. I should've had it. - The ice cream.

1637
01:08:19,801 --> 01:08:22,331
(That was satisfying shopping.)

1638
01:08:23,031 --> 01:08:25,941
(Humming)

1639
01:08:26,901 --> 01:08:29,411
(He excitedly reached home while humming.)

1640
01:08:30,441 --> 01:08:31,641
Gosh, this is crazy.

1641
01:08:32,541 --> 01:08:33,641
Gosh, it's crazy.

1642
01:08:36,681 --> 01:08:38,310
Bringing all of them inside...

1643
01:08:38,311 --> 01:08:39,951
- must be a lot of work. - It's really tiring.

1644
01:08:41,951 --> 01:08:45,351
(Struggling)

1645
01:08:45,991 --> 01:08:47,020
This is crazy.

1646
01:08:47,021 --> 01:08:48,021
(Stuff he carried home with great effort)

1647
01:08:48,191 --> 01:08:50,490
(Moving them 1 by 1 for now)

1648
01:08:50,491 --> 01:08:52,601
Thinking of organizing them... Gosh.

1649
01:08:53,161 --> 01:08:54,831
(Putting the cart he used outside)

1650
01:08:55,401 --> 01:08:58,671
(Here comes the second cart.)

1651
01:08:58,801 --> 01:09:00,201
It's the third cart.

1652
01:09:01,471 --> 01:09:02,840
(Pouring in stuff endlessly)

1653
01:09:02,841 --> 01:09:03,970
That's a lot.

1654
01:09:03,971 --> 01:09:05,211
(Pouring in stuff endlessly)

1655
01:09:06,581 --> 01:09:07,741
What's all this?

1656
01:09:07,841 --> 01:09:09,181
It looks like you newly moved in.

1657
01:09:09,911 --> 01:09:11,511
This is all because of Hue.

1658
01:09:15,481 --> 01:09:16,491
Gosh.

1659
01:09:17,321 --> 01:09:18,390
It's so hot.

1660
01:09:18,391 --> 01:09:21,321
(He's soaked in sweat when he only moved the stuff.)

1661
01:09:23,961 --> 01:09:26,601
(Going to the counter with the box in sight)

1662
01:09:27,531 --> 01:09:33,241
(He carefully opens it.)

1663
01:09:34,601 --> 01:09:38,071
(Pulling out a round lighting)

1664
01:09:38,611 --> 01:09:40,841
(He takes his time to read the manual.)

1665
01:09:41,581 --> 01:09:43,481
It's really easy. You just need to attach it.

1666
01:09:44,351 --> 01:09:45,480
Oh, this one?

1667
01:09:45,481 --> 01:09:46,580
(It looks like he's realized something.)

1668
01:09:46,581 --> 01:09:48,051
Oh, like this?

1669
01:09:48,881 --> 01:09:50,351
Oh, attach it like this?

1670
01:09:50,651 --> 01:09:52,120
(Laughing)

1671
01:09:52,121 --> 01:09:53,461
It's pretty.

1672
01:09:54,391 --> 01:09:55,561
It's simple.

1673
01:09:57,631 --> 01:10:00,601
(I should hurry up and turn it on.)

1674
01:10:03,001 --> 01:10:04,131
(Click)

1675
01:10:05,671 --> 01:10:06,901
(Impressed)

1676
01:10:07,571 --> 01:10:09,611
(Yes, this is the vibe I wanted!)

1677
01:10:11,511 --> 01:10:12,941
These will take a lot of work.

1678
01:10:13,711 --> 01:10:15,081
What's this? What was this again?

1679
01:10:15,141 --> 01:10:16,811
Oh, it's the iron piece. What is this?

1680
01:10:17,911 --> 01:10:18,981
(Oh, right. I got the Hue-style lighting.)

1681
01:10:19,351 --> 01:10:22,351
- That's Hue-style lighting. - Right. I'm familiar with that box.

1682
01:10:23,751 --> 01:10:25,151
It's just his style.

1683
01:10:25,621 --> 01:10:26,961
This is easy.

1684
01:10:27,321 --> 01:10:29,260
- He's become a kid. - I'm almost like a fanatic.

1685
01:10:29,261 --> 01:10:30,561
This is how it's done.

1686
01:10:30,991 --> 01:10:32,331
That's it. I'm done.

1687
01:10:33,131 --> 01:10:34,161
How fast.

1688
01:10:34,701 --> 01:10:35,701
Wait.

1689
01:10:36,001 --> 01:10:37,631
- Wait, this is... - What is it?

1690
01:10:37,801 --> 01:10:39,270
I should've bought a light bulb.

1691
01:10:39,271 --> 01:10:41,471
- You didn't get a bulb. - A light bulb.

1692
01:10:41,701 --> 01:10:43,741
Oh, you need to get a light bulb separately?

1693
01:10:44,671 --> 01:10:45,711
Didn't I get it?

1694
01:10:45,771 --> 01:10:48,341
It's really upsetting if you can't turn it on after assembling it.

1695
01:10:48,581 --> 01:10:50,351
- Right. You'd want to see it. - I didn't get the light bulb.

1696
01:10:51,651 --> 01:10:53,181
Does it have the same bulb as that one?

1697
01:10:54,951 --> 01:10:57,621
(Shall I take out the bulb?)

1698
01:11:01,791 --> 01:11:03,261
- No! - He broke it!

1699
01:11:05,256 --> 01:11:06,725
You wanted to take that out for the new lighting?

1700
01:11:06,726 --> 01:11:08,763
(Hyun Moo needs a light bulb for the Hue-style lighting.)

1701
01:11:11,796 --> 01:11:13,336
- No! - He broke it!

1702
01:11:14,006 --> 01:11:16,236
(Oh, no!)

1703
01:11:20,476 --> 01:11:21,700
(Broken into pieces)

1704
01:11:21,732 --> 01:11:24,032
The sound is really cruel.

1705
01:11:28,702 --> 01:11:31,441
I've not been able to...

1706
01:11:31,442 --> 01:11:32,972
assist Hyun Moo for a while.

1707
01:11:33,342 --> 01:11:35,742
I think this became a hobby in a strange way.

1708
01:11:36,442 --> 01:11:38,911
- What are you talking about? - There's a need...

1709
01:11:38,912 --> 01:11:41,282
for us to take care of Hyun Moo.

1710
01:11:41,482 --> 01:11:42,482
Are you saying I have no strength in my hands?

1711
01:11:42,483 --> 01:11:44,181
I think you keep focusing on other things...

1712
01:11:44,182 --> 01:11:45,882
- because you feel empty. - Empty?

1713
01:11:46,052 --> 01:11:47,721
I feel so worthless.

1714
01:11:47,722 --> 01:11:49,962
That's not it. I'm just worried.

1715
01:11:52,522 --> 01:11:55,532
You only used it for ten minutes after assembling it.

1716
01:11:58,202 --> 01:11:59,702
Gosh, seriously.

1717
01:12:01,272 --> 01:12:02,672
I like simple things.

1718
01:12:03,072 --> 01:12:07,442
I really liked it because it was such a pretty ball-shaped lamp.

1719
01:12:08,312 --> 01:12:11,342
When I turned it on, it was ecstatic.

1720
01:12:11,412 --> 01:12:12,982
It was the color I had in mind.

1721
01:12:13,112 --> 01:12:14,452
That exact shade of yellow.

1722
01:12:15,252 --> 01:12:17,782
I was so happy, but I broke it right away.

1723
01:12:19,452 --> 01:12:22,222
I was five times angrier than when I spilled pistachios.

1724
01:12:24,422 --> 01:12:26,192
It was such a shame.

1725
01:12:27,362 --> 01:12:28,892
I broke it as soon as I got it.

1726
01:12:28,992 --> 01:12:30,702
It lived less than a cicada would.

1727
01:12:31,802 --> 01:12:33,371
Those who know a style...

1728
01:12:33,372 --> 01:12:36,842
would display the lamp as is in broken pieces.

1729
01:12:37,102 --> 01:12:38,442
You'd just walk around even if you bleed.

1730
01:12:38,642 --> 01:12:41,672
If Hue walked around while bleeding,

1731
01:12:41,772 --> 01:12:43,681
you'd bleed too after saying, "This is it."

1732
01:12:43,682 --> 01:12:45,082
"So this is art."

1733
01:12:46,812 --> 01:12:49,251
(Taking the bulb out first)

1734
01:12:49,252 --> 01:12:50,252
(Sighing)

1735
01:12:51,722 --> 01:12:52,791
(Shall I check if it fits?)

1736
01:12:52,792 --> 01:12:54,122
He's still trying to fit it.

1737
01:12:55,822 --> 01:12:57,591
This one doesn't fit.

1738
01:12:57,592 --> 01:12:59,361
This isn't the one. It doesn't fit.

1739
01:12:59,362 --> 01:13:00,491
I shouldn't have taken it out.

1740
01:13:00,492 --> 01:13:03,032
They all have different socket sizes.

1741
01:13:03,402 --> 01:13:05,362
Why did I have to check?

1742
01:13:07,932 --> 01:13:10,972
(Upset)

1743
01:13:12,042 --> 01:13:13,342
Wait. It's like modern art.

1744
01:13:14,712 --> 01:13:15,742
Modern art.

1745
01:13:15,972 --> 01:13:17,011
(Displaying the broken piece like he knows a style)

1746
01:13:17,012 --> 01:13:18,182
Look. It's like modern art.

1747
01:13:18,612 --> 01:13:20,152
It fits perfectly. Right?

1748
01:13:20,952 --> 01:13:22,951
(Turning it on)

1749
01:13:22,952 --> 01:13:24,452
It's not bad.

1750
01:13:25,582 --> 01:13:26,751
It does look pretty.

1751
01:13:26,752 --> 01:13:27,851
(Hyun Moo brought something instead of a bulb.)

1752
01:13:27,852 --> 01:13:29,092
- What? - What is that?

1753
01:13:29,152 --> 01:13:31,992
You bought the exact same one as mine.

1754
01:13:32,592 --> 01:13:33,832
It's getting scary now, right?

1755
01:13:34,292 --> 01:13:36,332
I'm starting to feel a little bad.

1756
01:13:36,802 --> 01:13:38,831
I chose a different color because it was too creepy.

1757
01:13:38,832 --> 01:13:40,972
(It's a different color, so don't worry.)

1758
01:13:42,532 --> 01:13:45,341
(Transforming into the color Moomoo picked)

1759
01:13:45,342 --> 01:13:47,071
I've never seen one in pink.

1760
01:13:47,072 --> 01:13:48,312
It's incredible, isn't it?

1761
01:13:50,582 --> 01:13:53,452
(Stop right there, Hue-terior.)

1762
01:13:53,952 --> 01:13:55,282
Gosh, the color...

1763
01:13:55,982 --> 01:13:57,481
Should I have added a yellow one too?

1764
01:13:57,482 --> 01:13:58,722
(This isn't the vibe I wanted.)

1765
01:13:59,122 --> 01:14:00,791
The white one isn't so nice.

1766
01:14:00,792 --> 01:14:01,891
(He's losing the vibe of Hue-terior once again.)

1767
01:14:01,892 --> 01:14:03,192
Why did I get the one in white?

1768
01:14:03,462 --> 01:14:04,492
I should've chosen a different color.

1769
01:14:06,632 --> 01:14:10,432
(He kept assembling the rest while screaming.)

1770
01:14:11,562 --> 01:14:12,632
That one?

1771
01:14:12,932 --> 01:14:13,932
(His living room is a mess.)

1772
01:14:13,933 --> 01:14:16,002
I should assemble that later. First,

1773
01:14:16,842 --> 01:14:18,101
I should clear the room.

1774
01:14:18,102 --> 01:14:19,272
(Forget about the living room. Let's clear the studio first.)

1775
01:14:22,372 --> 01:14:23,982
Gosh, you still have too much stuff.

1776
01:14:24,112 --> 01:14:26,552
I think there's no space at all for the new items.

1777
01:14:27,782 --> 01:14:30,982
I should clear this part out neatly.

1778
01:14:31,182 --> 01:14:32,522
And I'll paint here.

1779
01:14:34,192 --> 01:14:35,521
(Moving)

1780
01:14:35,522 --> 01:14:36,962
I should move these.

1781
01:14:37,222 --> 01:14:38,662
What? There's a lighting too?

1782
01:14:39,362 --> 01:14:41,031
What? Oh, it's one that CODE KUNST gave me.

1783
01:14:41,032 --> 01:14:43,532
- You bought that from my place. - You had a lighting.

1784
01:14:45,232 --> 01:14:49,002
(Convinced by CODE KUNST's pitch 3 years ago,)

1785
01:14:50,242 --> 01:14:54,242
(he bought this lighting like fate.)

1786
01:14:55,312 --> 01:14:56,542
I had one that was similar.

1787
01:14:56,842 --> 01:14:58,811
I had to replace it with the one I broke.

1788
01:14:58,812 --> 01:15:00,252
(How lucky. I should use this instead of the broken lamp.)

1789
01:15:01,112 --> 01:15:03,182
I almost bought the same one earlier.

1790
01:15:03,352 --> 01:15:04,382
I must be crazy.

1791
01:15:05,522 --> 01:15:06,852
Goodness.

1792
01:15:07,422 --> 01:15:09,152
- Gosh! No! - Gosh! No!

1793
01:15:11,922 --> 01:15:12,992
(Crash)

1794
01:15:15,192 --> 01:15:16,232
(Dropping)

1795
01:15:17,562 --> 01:15:18,931
Seriously...

1796
01:15:18,932 --> 01:15:21,102
(Feeling devastated)

1797
01:15:22,572 --> 01:15:23,601
(Shaking)

1798
01:15:23,602 --> 01:15:25,571
It's really annoying to clean that up.

1799
01:15:25,572 --> 01:15:27,512
I'll visit you at home from time to time.

1800
01:15:27,942 --> 01:15:29,371
I'm sorry I didn't pay much attention to you.

1801
01:15:29,372 --> 01:15:30,712
- Look after me. - Yes.

1802
01:15:32,342 --> 01:15:35,112
(Flopping)

